 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/en/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # secret_key is used for authenticating requests to the Scaleway API (mandatory).
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/identity-and-access-management/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/
+  - secret_key: "..."
+
+    # Exactly one of project_id or organization_id must be set, in order to select
+    # the instances to discover.
+
+    # project_id is the id of the Scaleway project to discover instances from.
+    #
+    # project_id: "..."
+
+    # organization_id is the id of the Scaleway organization to discover instances from.
+    #
+    # organization_id: "..."
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway zone to discover instances in.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/console/account/reference-content/products-availability/
+    #
+    # zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # api_url is an optional Scaleway API url.
+    #
+    # api_url: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+
+
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<public_ipv4>:<port>`, where `<public_ipv4>` is a public ipv4 address of the instance (or its private ipv4 address, if the instance has no public IP),
+while `<port>` is the port specified in the `scaleway_sd_configs` (default port is `80`).
+
+Only instances in the `running` state are discovered.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_boot_type`: the boot type of the instance, such as `local` or `bootscript`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the unique id of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the id of the organization the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private ipv4 address of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the id of the project the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public ipv4 address of the instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv6`: the public ipv6 address of the instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the state of the instance, e.g. `running`, `stopped`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma-separated list of tags assigned to the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the [commercial type](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/instances/reference-content/choosing-instance-type/) of the instance, e.g. `DEV1-S`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the [zone](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/console/account/reference-content/products-availability/) the instance is located in.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag, default: 30s.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
